        ]
      ],
      "id": "pz859ts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h0t647y",
      "content": "• Judges retire at age 62."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "peto5yl",
      "content": "• They can resign to the President."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7upfmvz",
      "content": "• They can be removed through impeachment."
    },
    {
      "id": "aegnbjk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Jurisdiction of High Court"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fqrq2sy",
      "content": "Original, Appellate, Writ, and Supervisory jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "id": "42dd78m",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Types of Writs"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Writ jurisdiction of the High Court under Article 226 is wider than that of the Supreme Court under Article 32, as it extends to ordinary legal rights.",
        "High Court judges are appointed by the President, not the Governor, though the Governor is consulted.",
        "A High Court judge tenders resignation to the President of India."
      ],
      "id": "44ltt9r"
    },
